# examples/llm_wiki — environment template. cp .env.example .env, then edit.
#
# run_wiki.py loads this file before building the agent (run_wiki.py:33).
#
# Uncomment and fill in what you need; leave the rest commented. An empty
# value ("OPENAI_API_KEY=") still registers the name in os.environ, and
# models/model_factory.py checks presence rather than truth, so a blank line
# hides the "key is required" error behind a 401 from the provider.

# --- Required: agent.yaml is provider: openai, model: gpt-4o ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=          <- uncomment and paste your key

# --- Alternatives, if you repoint agent.yaml's provider/endpoint ---
# No key for a local vLLM or litellm server; set endpoint.url in agent.yaml.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=       needs an OpenAI-compatible proxy — see README.md

# --- Optional ---
# SDK_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG
